---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getSections } from '../../lib/content';

const sections = await getSections();
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Software engineer in Singapore. Mathematics with Computing graduate from TARUMT, previously Java in banking, now building AI agents and data platforms for building automation."
>
  <article class="page">
    <header class="page__header">
      <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal="fade">About</p>
      <h1 class="page__title" data-reveal="split-lines">Who I am</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="page__body">
      <section data-reveal="fade-up">
        <p class="lead">Software Engineer</p>
        <p>
          My name is Lee Cheng Zhan. I was born in 2000, I'm Malaysian, and I live
          and work in Singapore on an Employment Pass. I build production AI agents
          and the data platforms behind them, for building automation.
        </p>
        <p>
          I hold a degree in Mathematics with Computing from Tunku Abdul Rahman
          University of Management and Technology (TARUMT), graduating in 2022 with
          a CGPA of 3.63. The programme paired mathematics as the major with
          computer science as the minor — an unusual combination, and the reason I
          reach for the analytical framing of a problem before the code. My final
          year project modelled <a href="/work/school-fyp">baseball as a two-player
          zero-sum game</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section data-reveal="fade-up">
        <h2>Career journey</h2>
        <p>
          I started in January 2022 at AceAtt Sdn. Bhd. in Kuala Lumpur, a software
          house whose customers are banks. Two client projects in that time:
          <a href="/work/alliance-bank">Java web applications for Alliance Bank</a>,
          and a <a href="/work/bank-negara">regulatory reporting module</a> for Bank
          Negara Malaysia, the central bank. Client-facing from the start, and the
          first place I learned what a production issue costs when the production in
          question is a bank's.
        </p>
        <p>
          Since June 2023 I've been at Primustech in Singapore, in building
          automation. I arrived on the Java side of a
          <a href="/work/bms-platform">Building Management System</a>, then built
          the <a href="/work/cloud-data-platform">cloud data platform</a> that
          unified equipment and sensor data across buildings and vendors, and now
          design and ship the <a href="/work/ai-agent-bms">AI agents</a> that reason
          over it.
        </p>
        <p>
          Three years in, the through-line is that I own what I build end to end —
          development, deployment and CI/CD — solo or in a small team. That is the
          part I want to keep doing, in AI agent and backend engineering.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section data-reveal="fade-up">
        <h2>What I work with</h2>
        <dl class="skills">
          <div>
            <dt>Languages</dt>
            <dd>Python · JavaScript · TypeScript · Java</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>AI / agent</dt>
            <dd>
              Multi-agent orchestration · agentic RAG · prompt engineering ·
              function calling · LLM observability and tracing (Langfuse,
              OpenTelemetry)
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Frameworks</dt>
            <dd>Agno · FastAPI · Spring Boot · MyBatis · Hibernate · Vert.x · Express · React</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Cloud / DevOps</dt>
            <dd>
              GCP (Cloud Run, Cloud Build, VM instances, Cloud Storage, Secret
              Manager) · Docker · Terraform · CI/CD · Git
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Databases</dt>
            <dd>PostgreSQL · MySQL · MongoDB · Redis · Milvus · ClickHouse · FalkorDB</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
        <p>
          I also speak Mandarin, English and Malay, and worked through the Complete
          2024 Web Development Bootcamp on Udemy to fill in the parts of the stack
          that backend work never forces you to learn properly.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section data-reveal="fade-up">
        <h2>Beyond work</h2>
        <p>
          I play football competitively and run marathons. The running is mostly an
          exercise in doing something boring for a long time without negotiating
          with yourself about it, which turns out to be a transferable skill.
        </p>
        <p>
          I travel with a camera and make the occasional vlog. Filming, editing and
          narrating footage has done more for how I explain things than any course
          I've taken.
        </p>
        <p>
          Before any of the software, I spent seven years as a 24 Festival drummer
          with JB Drum — 70-plus performances across Malaysia, Singapore and China
          between 2013 and 2020, and teaching workshops to new players. Twenty-four
          drums in formation is an unusual first lesson in distributed systems:
          nobody can hear the whole thing from where they're standing, and it still
          has to stay in time.
        </p>
        <p>
          I also worked part-time as a promoter and salesman from 2018 to 2021, with
          Synmax Event and Jasler Enterprise, which is where I learned to change how
          I explain something depending on who is listening.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <nav class="subnav" aria-label="About sections">
      <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal="fade">Read more</p>
      <ul class="subnav__list">
        {
          sections.map((section, i) => (
            <li data-reveal="fade-up" data-reveal-delay={String(i * 0.06)}>
              <a href={`/about/${section.id}`} class="subnav__card">
                <h3>{section.data.title}</h3>
                <p>{section.data.summary}</p>
              </a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </nav>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  @reference "#styles";

  .page {
    @apply mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-20 lg:py-28;
  }

  .page__header {
    @apply mb-12 flex flex-col gap-3;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    @apply font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-fg-meta;
  }

  .page__title {
    @apply text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight lg:text-5xl;
  }

  .page__body {
    @apply flex flex-col gap-12;
  }

  .page__body section {
    @apply flex flex-col gap-4;
  }

  .lead {
    @apply text-lg text-fg-meta;
  }

  .page__body h2 {
    @apply text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight;
  }

  .page__body p {
    @apply leading-relaxed text-fg-body;
  }

  .page__body a {
    @apply text-accent underline decoration-accent/30 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-accent;
  }

  /* Stacks below sm so the label never squeezes the value into a column of one
     word per line — the narrow-viewport audit in CLAUDE.md has not happened yet,
     so this starts single-column and earns its second one at 640px. */
  .skills {
    @apply flex flex-col gap-4;
  }

  .skills > div {
    @apply flex flex-col gap-1 border-t border-line pt-4 sm:grid sm:grid-cols-[8rem_1fr] sm:gap-4;
  }

  .skills dt {
    @apply font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-fg-meta;
  }

  .skills dd {
    @apply m-0 leading-relaxed text-fg-body;
  }

  .subnav {
    @apply mt-20 flex flex-col gap-4 border-t border-line pt-12;
  }

  .subnav__list {
    @apply grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2;
  }

  .subnav__card {
    @apply flex h-full flex-col gap-2 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-surface p-5 transition-all duration-300;
    @apply hover:-translate-y-1 hover:border-accent/40 hover:shadow-md;
  }

  .subnav__card h3 {
    @apply font-semibold text-fg;
  }

  .subnav__card p {
    @apply text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted;
  }
</style>
